ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Core_Concept a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "From \"Noise\" to \"Information\"" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Core_Concept ex:the_shift "In this context, we treat speckle as a sophisticated \"fingerprint.\" If you know how the speckle pattern behaves, you can mathematically reconstruct the object or environment that caused it." .
<< ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Core_Concept ex:the_shift "In this context, we treat speckle as a sophisticated \"fingerprint.\" If you know how the speckle pattern behaves, you can mathematically reconstruct the object or environment that caused it." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Core_Concept ex:the_problem "Traditional \"random\" diffusers (like frosted glass) are uncontrolled. You get a random pattern, but you can't tune it for specific sensing tasks." .
<< ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Core_Concept ex:the_problem "Traditional \"random\" diffusers (like frosted glass) are uncontrolled. You get a random pattern, but you can't tune it for specific sensing tasks." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Role_of_Metamaterials_The_Encoder a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "2\\. The Role of Metamaterials (\"The Encoder\")" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Role_of_Metamaterials_The_Encoder ex:engineered_disorder "Instead of relying on a naturally rough surface, we use a metamaterial surface designed to scatter light in a _precisely known_ but complex way." .
<< ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Role_of_Metamaterials_The_Encoder ex:engineered_disorder "Instead of relying on a naturally rough surface, we use a metamaterial surface designed to scatter light in a _precisely known_ but complex way." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Role_of_Metamaterials_The_Encoder ex:compressive_sensing "Metamaterials allow us to \"compress\" visual data before it even hits the sensor. A single \"random\" speckle measurement can contain spatial, spectral, and depth information all mixed together." .
<< ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Role_of_Metamaterials_The_Encoder ex:compressive_sensing "Metamaterials allow us to \"compress\" visual data before it even hits the sensor. A single \"random\" speckle measurement can contain spatial, spectral, and depth information all mixed together." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Role_of_Metamaterials_The_Encoder ex:form_factor "This replaces bulky prism or lens systems with a flat, microscopic chip." .
<< ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_The_Role_of_Metamaterials_The_Encoder ex:form_factor "This replaces bulky prism or lens systems with a flat, microscopic chip." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_Fast_Optical_Sensing_The_Decoder a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "3\\. Fast Optical Sensing (\"The Decoder\")" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_Fast_Optical_Sensing_The_Decoder ex:fewer_measurements_higher_speed "Because the metamaterial \"mixes\" the information so efficiently, you need fewer snapshots to reconstruct the image. If you only need 10% of the usual data to build an image, you can effectively image 10x faster." .
<< ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_Fast_Optical_Sensing_The_Decoder ex:fewer_measurements_higher_speed "Because the metamaterial \"mixes\" the information so efficiently, you need fewer snapshots to reconstruct the image. If you only need 10% of the usual data to build an image, you can effectively image 10x faster." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_Fast_Optical_Sensing_The_Decoder ex:dynamic_speckle_analysis "For sensing vibrations or blood flow, we don't need a full image. We just track how fast the speckle pattern \"boils\" or changes. Metamaterials can enhance contrast here, making sensors hyper-sensitive to micro-movements (nanometer scale) at very high speeds (kHz to MHz rates)." .
<< ex:Speckle_Metamaterials_and_Fast_Sensing_Fast_Optical_Sensing_The_Decoder ex:dynamic_speckle_analysis "For sensing vibrations or blood flow, we don't need a full image. We just track how fast the speckle pattern \"boils\" or changes. Metamaterials can enhance contrast here, making sensors hyper-sensitive to micro-movements (nanometer scale) at very high speeds (kHz to MHz rates)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
