ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Photons_Particle_Nature ex:for_fog ", the exact same absorption/re-emission process happens on the surface of each individual water droplet. Because the droplets are tiny, suspended, and randomly oriented, they re-emit the photons in all directions, which is why fog scatters light and you can see the beam's path. A wall just does this on a flat, collective surface." .
