ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:what_it_is "A module within the NEORV32, a complete open-source RISC-V processor. The TRNG is a standalone peripheral that can be extracted and used in your own design." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:what_it_is "A module within the NEORV32, a complete open-source RISC-V processor. The TRNG is a standalone peripheral that can be extracted and used in your own design." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:why_its_a_good_choice "It's a complete, well-documented package. It features a conditioner based on a Galois LFSR (Linear-Feedback Shift Register) and includes the necessary control logic and health monitors required by standards like NIST SP 800-90B. You would bypass its built-in ring oscillator entropy sources and feed in your external source." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:why_its_a_good_choice "It's a complete, well-documented package. It features a conditioner based on a Galois LFSR (Linear-Feedback Shift Register) and includes the necessary control logic and health monitors required by standards like NIST SP 800-90B. You would bypass its built-in ring oscillator entropy sources and feed in your external source." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:license "Permissive (3-clause BSD)." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:license "Permissive (3-clause BSD)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:sha256_core "(many are available on sites like OpenCores)." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:sha256_core "(many are available on sites like OpenCores)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:how_it_works "You collect a buffer of raw, noisy bits from your sensor and then feed the entire buffer through a SHA-256 hash function. The resulting 256-bit hash is your random output. This is a very effective way to eliminate bias and increase the entropy density of your output." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Conclusion ex:how_it_works "You collect a buffer of raw, noisy bits from your sensor and then feed the entire buffer through a SHA-256 hash function. The resulting 256-bit hash is your random output. This is a very effective way to eliminate bias and increase the entropy density of your output." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
