ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:higher_dimensionality "With two LEDs, you have one primary interference relationship. With four or eight LEDs, you create a vastly more complex, multi-dimensional interference pattern. This makes the \"raw\" bitstream significantly closer to 50/50 distribution before it even reaches the GPU." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:higher_dimensionality "With two LEDs, you have one primary interference relationship. With four or eight LEDs, you create a vastly more complex, multi-dimensional interference pattern. This makes the \"raw\" bitstream significantly closer to 50/50 distribution before it even reaches the GPU." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:redundancy_and_reliability "If one LED burns out in a two-LED system, the entropy drops to near zero (you just have a steady light). In an 8-LED array, the system can detect a single failure via the NIST health checks, alert you, and continue operating with 7/8ths of its entropy capacity." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:redundancy_and_reliability "If one LED burns out in a two-LED system, the entropy drops to near zero (you just have a steady light). In an 8-LED array, the system can detect a single failure via the NIST health checks, alert you, and continue operating with 7/8ths of its entropy capacity." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:increased_bandwidth_of_chaos "More sources mean more independent phase fluctuations occurring simultaneously. This allows you to sample the light at even higher frequencies (higher GS/s) without the samples becoming \"correlated\" (predictable based on the previous sample)." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:increased_bandwidth_of_chaos "More sources mean more independent phase fluctuations occurring simultaneously. This allows you to sample the light at even higher frequencies (higher GS/s) without the samples becoming \"correlated\" (predictable based on the previous sample)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:parallel_ingestion "Each NIC can capture a different \"view\" of the entropy. You could have one fiber bundle from the LED array split into four branches, each feeding a different NIC. This quadruples the raw data rate flowing into your mining rig." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:parallel_ingestion "Each NIC can capture a different \"view\" of the entropy. You could have one fiber bundle from the LED array split into four branches, each feeding a different NIC. This quadruples the raw data rate flowing into your mining rig." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:segmented_entropy_pools "Multiple NICs allow you to provide \"Hardware-Isolated Entropy.\" You could dedicate NIC #1 to \"High-Security Cryptographic Keys\" (low volume, ultra-high processing) and NIC #2 to \"Scientific Simulations\" (high volume, faster/lighter whitening)." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:segmented_entropy_pools "Multiple NICs allow you to provide \"Hardware-Isolated Entropy.\" You could dedicate NIC #1 to \"High-Security Cryptographic Keys\" (low volume, ultra-high processing) and NIC #2 to \"Scientific Simulations\" (high volume, faster/lighter whitening)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:bypassing_pcie_congestion "By using multiple NICs across different PCIe slots, you distribute the \"firehose\" of data across the motherboard's different PCIe lanes, preventing a single bus from becoming a bottleneck for the GPUs." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_Aggregation_and_Output ex:bypassing_pcie_congestion "By using multiple NICs across different PCIe slots, you distribute the \"firehose\" of data across the motherboard's different PCIe lanes, preventing a single bus from becoming a bottleneck for the GPUs." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
