ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_Core_Component a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "The N:M Multimode Star Coupler" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_Core_Component ex:how_it_works "In a 4x4 Star Coupler, four input fibers are fused together in a single \"mixing zone.\" Light from any one of the 4 LEDs is distributed equally (roughly 25% each) across all 4 output NIC ports." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_Core_Component ex:how_it_works "In a 4x4 Star Coupler, four input fibers are fused together in a single \"mixing zone.\" Light from any one of the 4 LEDs is distributed equally (roughly 25% each) across all 4 output NIC ports." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_Core_Component ex:the_mixing_advantage "If you use 4 LEDs, each of your 4 NIC ports receives a \"physical sum\" of 4 independent chaotic sources. This dramatically increases the entropy density and makes the system nearly impossible to \"blind\" or predict, even if one source is compromised." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_Core_Component ex:the_mixing_advantage "If you use 4 LEDs, each of your 4 NIC ports receives a \"physical sum\" of 4 independent chaotic sources. This dramatically increases the entropy density and makes the system nearly impossible to \"blind\" or predict, even if one source is compromised." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
