ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_LowCost_Mixing ex:the_method "Instead of \"pigtailing\" (permanently attaching) one LED to one fiber, you aim multiple discrete LEDs into the open end of a single, thick fiber (like a 1mm core POF)." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_LowCost_Mixing ex:the_method "Instead of \"pigtailing\" (permanently attaching) one LED to one fiber, you aim multiple discrete LEDs into the open end of a single, thick fiber (like a 1mm core POF)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_LowCost_Mixing ex:why_its_simpler "You don't need precision alignment. You can 3D print a small housing that holds 4 standard 5mm LEDs and points them all into the face of one thick fiber. The \"mixing\" happens naturally as the light bounces down the large-core fiber." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_The_LowCost_Mixing ex:why_its_simpler "You don't need precision alignment. You can 3D print a small housing that holds 4 standard 5mm LEDs and points them all into the face of one thick fiber. The \"mixing\" happens naturally as the light bounces down the large-core fiber." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
