ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_How_Modern_Systems_Make_it_Possible a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "2\\. How Modern Systems Make it Possible" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_How_Modern_Systems_Make_it_Possible ex:dense_wavelength_division_multiplexing_dwdm "The quantum signal is placed in a very specific \"channel\" (wavelength) far away from the noisy classical channels. Usually, the quantum channel is placed in the" .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_How_Modern_Systems_Make_it_Possible ex:dense_wavelength_division_multiplexing_dwdm "The quantum signal is placed in a very specific \"channel\" (wavelength) far away from the noisy classical channels. Usually, the quantum channel is placed in the" >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_How_Modern_Systems_Make_it_Possible ex:ultranarrow_filtering "At the receiving end, high-finesse filters (like Bragg gratings) act as \"narrow tunnels,\" allowing only the specific quantum frequency through while blocking 99.99% of the classical noise." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_How_Modern_Systems_Make_it_Possible ex:ultranarrow_filtering "At the receiving end, high-finesse filters (like Bragg gratings) act as \"narrow tunnels,\" allowing only the specific quantum frequency through while blocking 99.99% of the classical noise." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_How_Modern_Systems_Make_it_Possible ex:temporal_synchronization_timegating "Since classical data is pulsed, the quantum receiver only \"looks\" for photons in the nanosecond-scale gaps between classical pulses, effectively dodging the noise." .
<< ex:Red_and_Blue_Laser_Beam_Mixing_How_Modern_Systems_Make_it_Possible ex:temporal_synchronization_timegating "Since classical data is pulsed, the quantum receiver only \"looks\" for photons in the nanosecond-scale gaps between classical pulses, effectively dodging the noise." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
