    rdfs:label "2\\. The \"Confinement\" Requirement" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_The_Confinement_Requirement ex:the_setup "The material is typically covered with a sacrificial layer (like black paint or aluminum foil) and a confinement medium (like water or glass). When the laser hits, the sacrificial layer turns into plasma, and the water/glass forces that plasma expansion _downward_ into the material." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_The_Confinement_Requirement ex:the_setup "The material is typically covered with a sacrificial layer (like black paint or aluminum foil) and a confinement medium (like water or glass). When the laser hits, the sacrificial layer turns into plasma, and the water/glass forces that plasma expansion _downward_ into the material." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_The_Confinement_Requirement ex:manufacturing_nightmare "wrapping a continuously moving, microscopic A-CNT filament in a sacrificial layer and a confinement layer (water jet or glass slide), then hitting it with a laser, is extremely difficult compared to simply treating a flat sheet (roll-to-roll)." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_The_Confinement_Requirement ex:manufacturing_nightmare "wrapping a continuously moving, microscopic A-CNT filament in a sacrificial layer and a confinement layer (water jet or glass slide), then hitting it with a laser, is extremely difficult compared to simply treating a flat sheet (roll-to-roll)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
