ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_The_New_Bottleneck ex:the_issue "Lignin is a thermal insulator. If you stack 50 layers of ribbon, the heat generated in the _middle_ layers cannot easily escape to the surface to be cooled. The center of your ribbon stack could overheat and degrade the vitrimer." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_The_New_Bottleneck ex:the_issue "Lignin is a thermal insulator. If you stack 50 layers of ribbon, the heat generated in the _middle_ layers cannot easily escape to the surface to be cooled. The center of your ribbon stack could overheat and degrade the vitrimer." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_The_New_Bottleneck ex:the_engineering_fix "You may need to limit the stack height or interleave \"thermal wicks\" (perhaps thicker graphene layers without lignin) to pull heat out to the edges." .
