ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_001_method_for_synthesis_of_magnetic_cermet_conductor_skins "A method for manufacturing a high-frequency conductive composite, comprising the application of a lignin-based slurry containing iron oxide nanoparticles onto a metal substrate, followed by Flash Joule Heating (FJH) to simultaneously reduce the iron oxide to metallic nodules and graphitize the lignin into turbostratic graphene, resulting in a magnetically aligned, oxidation-resistant conductive skin." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_001_method_for_synthesis_of_magnetic_cermet_conductor_skins "A method for manufacturing a high-frequency conductive composite, comprising the application of a lignin-based slurry containing iron oxide nanoparticles onto a metal substrate, followed by Flash Joule Heating (FJH) to simultaneously reduce the iron oxide to metallic nodules and graphitize the lignin into turbostratic graphene, resulting in a magnetically aligned, oxidation-resistant conductive skin." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_002_structure_of_a_hybrid_aluminumscandiumcarbon_cable "A composite electrical cable comprising a central load-bearing core of aluminum-scandium alloy derived from bauxite residue, a chemically bonded interface layer of flash-induced graphene-cermet, and an outer insulating jacket of magnetically aligned vertical graphene or boron nitride nanotubes embedded in a lignin-vitrimer matrix, configured to decouple mechanical load bearing from high-frequency current transport." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_002_structure_of_a_hybrid_aluminumscandiumcarbon_cable "A composite electrical cable comprising a central load-bearing core of aluminum-scandium alloy derived from bauxite residue, a chemically bonded interface layer of flash-induced graphene-cermet, and an outer insulating jacket of magnetically aligned vertical graphene or boron nitride nanotubes embedded in a lignin-vitrimer matrix, configured to decouple mechanical load bearing from high-frequency current transport." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_003_zerowaste_manufacturing_of_electrical_components_from_bauxite_residue "A continuous manufacturing process wherein bauxite residue (red mud) is subjected to hydrogen plasma reduction to yield iron nodules, scandium-enriched slag, and alumino-silicate microspheres, which are subsequently processed in-line to form, respectively, magnetic alignment particles, conductor alloy dopants, and ceramic fireproofing fillers for a single electrical cable product." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_003_zerowaste_manufacturing_of_electrical_components_from_bauxite_residue "A continuous manufacturing process wherein bauxite residue (red mud) is subjected to hydrogen plasma reduction to yield iron nodules, scandium-enriched slag, and alumino-silicate microspheres, which are subsequently processed in-line to form, respectively, magnetic alignment particles, conductor alloy dopants, and ceramic fireproofing fillers for a single electrical cable product." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_004_selfhealing_vitrimer_insulation_system_via_induction_heating "An electrical insulation system comprising a dynamic covalent polymer (vitrimer) doped with ferromagnetic nanoparticles, configured to undergo localized reversible depolymerization and reflow upon exposure to an external alternating magnetic field, thereby repairing micro-cracks or enabling seamless fusion splicing without external adhesives." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_004_selfhealing_vitrimer_insulation_system_via_induction_heating "An electrical insulation system comprising a dynamic covalent polymer (vitrimer) doped with ferromagnetic nanoparticles, configured to undergo localized reversible depolymerization and reflow upon exposure to an external alternating magnetic field, thereby repairing micro-cracks or enabling seamless fusion splicing without external adhesives." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_005_radial_thermal_management_via_magnetically_aligned_nanostructures "An electrical cable jacket comprising high-aspect-ratio thermally conductive particles (graphene, CNTs, or BNNTs) magnetically locked in a radial orientation relative to the cable axis within a polymer matrix, creating a direct thermal path from the conductor core to the ambient environment while maintaining electrical isolation between the core and the exterior." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_005_radial_thermal_management_via_magnetically_aligned_nanostructures "An electrical cable jacket comprising high-aspect-ratio thermally conductive particles (graphene, CNTs, or BNNTs) magnetically locked in a radial orientation relative to the cable axis within a polymer matrix, creating a direct thermal path from the conductor core to the ambient environment while maintaining electrical isolation between the core and the exterior." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_006_insitu_capacitor_power_buffering_for_pulse_heating_manufacturing "A power management system for flash joule heating manufacturing, utilizing supercapacitors constructed from carbonized bast fiber electrodes and hydrothermal carbon nanospheres to provide millisecond-scale high-current discharge pulses, decoupling the manufacturing load from the utility grid." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_006_insitu_capacitor_power_buffering_for_pulse_heating_manufacturing "A power management system for flash joule heating manufacturing, utilizing supercapacitors constructed from carbonized bast fiber electrodes and hydrothermal carbon nanospheres to provide millisecond-scale high-current discharge pulses, decoupling the manufacturing load from the utility grid." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_007_distributed_sensing_via_laserinduced_graphene_patterns_on_cable_insulation "A \"smart cable\" architecture wherein the outer surface of a lignin-based insulation jacket is selectively laser-scribed to form a nitrogen-doped laser-induced graphene (N-LIG) sensor network, configured to monitor distributed temperature, mechanical strain, and dielectric integrity in real-time without additional discrete sensors." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Intellectual_Property_Claims ex:lignolux_007_distributed_sensing_via_laserinduced_graphene_patterns_on_cable_insulation "A \"smart cable\" architecture wherein the outer surface of a lignin-based insulation jacket is selectively laser-scribed to form a nitrogen-doped laser-induced graphene (N-LIG) sensor network, configured to monitor distributed temperature, mechanical strain, and dielectric integrity in real-time without additional discrete sensors." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
