    rdfs:label "**Advanced Thermal & Mechanical Systems**" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Advanced_Thermal_Mechanical_Systems ex:lignolux_009_phasechange_sweating_cable_insulation "A thermal management system for electrical conductors comprising a porous lignin-derived aerogel jacket impregnated with a phase-change material (PCM) such as polyethylene glycol or bio-wax, configured to absorb transient thermal spikes via latent heat fusion during peak motor loads and release heat during off-peak cycles, effectively increasing the short-duration ampacity of the conductor without increasing steady-state temperature." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Advanced_Thermal_Mechanical_Systems ex:lignolux_009_phasechange_sweating_cable_insulation "A thermal management system for electrical conductors comprising a porous lignin-derived aerogel jacket impregnated with a phase-change material (PCM) such as polyethylene glycol or bio-wax, configured to absorb transient thermal spikes via latent heat fusion during peak motor loads and release heat during off-peak cycles, effectively increasing the short-duration ampacity of the conductor without increasing steady-state temperature." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Advanced_Thermal_Mechanical_Systems ex:lignolux_010_centrifugal_microfluidic_cooling_wick "An active cooling architecture for rotating electrical machines (motors/generators) wherein the winding insulation consists of a continuous open-cell lignin aerogel network, configured to act as a micro-fluidic wick that draws dielectric cooling oil from the stator core and pumps it radially outward via centrifugal force, thereby actively transporting heat away from the conductor surface through the insulation layer." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Advanced_Thermal_Mechanical_Systems ex:lignolux_010_centrifugal_microfluidic_cooling_wick "An active cooling architecture for rotating electrical machines (motors/generators) wherein the winding insulation consists of a continuous open-cell lignin aerogel network, configured to act as a micro-fluidic wick that draws dielectric cooling oil from the stator core and pumps it radially outward via centrifugal force, thereby actively transporting heat away from the conductor surface through the insulation layer." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
