ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Electromagnetic_Operational_Features ex:lignolux_014_intrinsic_emi_shielding_via_magnetic_cermet_skin "An electromagnetic interference (EMI) suppression system for high-voltage cables, wherein the conductive skin layer comprises a ferromagnetic cermet (iron nanoparticles embedded in turbostratic graphene), possessing high magnetic permeability to absorb and dissipate high-frequency noise generated by inverter switching, thereby acting as a distributed Faraday cage without an external braid." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Electromagnetic_Operational_Features ex:lignolux_014_intrinsic_emi_shielding_via_magnetic_cermet_skin "An electromagnetic interference (EMI) suppression system for high-voltage cables, wherein the conductive skin layer comprises a ferromagnetic cermet (iron nanoparticles embedded in turbostratic graphene), possessing high magnetic permeability to absorb and dissipate high-frequency noise generated by inverter switching, thereby acting as a distributed Faraday cage without an external braid." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Electromagnetic_Operational_Features ex:lignolux_015_endless_cable_splicing_via_inductionactivated_fusion "A method for field-splicing hybrid metal-ceramic cables, wherein the cable ends are joined within a portable induction chamber that simultaneously melts the aluminum alloy core and reflows the thermoplastic vitrimer-cermet skin, utilizing the embedded iron nanoparticles as localized heating elements to fuse the interface into a homogeneous, hermetically sealed continuum." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Electromagnetic_Operational_Features ex:lignolux_015_endless_cable_splicing_via_inductionactivated_fusion "A method for field-splicing hybrid metal-ceramic cables, wherein the cable ends are joined within a portable induction chamber that simultaneously melts the aluminum alloy core and reflows the thermoplastic vitrimer-cermet skin, utilizing the embedded iron nanoparticles as localized heating elements to fuse the interface into a homogeneous, hermetically sealed continuum." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Electromagnetic_Operational_Features ex:lignolux_016_radiationhardened_ceramicpolymer_composite "An insulation formulation for high-radiation environments (e.g., fusion reactors), comprising a lignin-vitrimer matrix heavily loaded with plasma-spheroidized alumino-silicate microspheres derived from bauxite residue slag, configured to maintain dielectric strength and mechanical flexibility under neutron flux by dissipating ionization energy through the ceramic filler network." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_Electromagnetic_Operational_Features ex:lignolux_016_radiationhardened_ceramicpolymer_composite "An insulation formulation for high-radiation environments (e.g., fusion reactors), comprising a lignin-vitrimer matrix heavily loaded with plasma-spheroidized alumino-silicate microspheres derived from bauxite residue slag, configured to maintain dielectric strength and mechanical flexibility under neutron flux by dissipating ionization energy through the ceramic filler network." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
