ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_New_Busbar_Process_Claims_Method_A_B ex:lignolux_022_method_for_localized_superplastic_forming_of_scandiumaluminum_components "A manufacturing method for bending high-stiffness aluminum-scandium alloy busbars, comprising the localized rapid heating of a target deformation zone to the superplastic transition temperature (~450°C) via a high-frequency induction coil, followed by mechanical bending to a radius less than the component thickness, and immediate air-quenching to re-precipitate scandium trialuminide ( $Al_{3}Sc$ ) particles, thereby locking the grain structure in the bent geometry." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_New_Busbar_Process_Claims_Method_A_B ex:lignolux_022_method_for_localized_superplastic_forming_of_scandiumaluminum_components "A manufacturing method for bending high-stiffness aluminum-scandium alloy busbars, comprising the localized rapid heating of a target deformation zone to the superplastic transition temperature (~450°C) via a high-frequency induction coil, followed by mechanical bending to a radius less than the component thickness, and immediate air-quenching to re-precipitate scandium trialuminide ( $Al_{3}Sc$ ) particles, thereby locking the grain structure in the bent geometry." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_New_Busbar_Process_Claims_Method_A_B ex:lignolux_023_method_for_geometric_locking_of_laminated_conductors_via_induction_fusion "A process for manufacturing rigid, complex-geometry electrical busbars, comprising the steps of: (a) stacking a plurality of aluminum-scandium plates with an inter-layer solid lubricant; (b) mechanically bending the loose stack to induce shear slip between layers; and (c) subjecting the ends or edges of the bent stack to an induction welding field to fuse the layers into a monolithic solid, thereby permanently fixing the shear displacement and converting the flexible stack into a rigid structural component." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_New_Busbar_Process_Claims_Method_A_B ex:lignolux_023_method_for_geometric_locking_of_laminated_conductors_via_induction_fusion "A process for manufacturing rigid, complex-geometry electrical busbars, comprising the steps of: (a) stacking a plurality of aluminum-scandium plates with an inter-layer solid lubricant; (b) mechanically bending the loose stack to induce shear slip between layers; and (c) subjecting the ends or edges of the bent stack to an induction welding field to fuse the layers into a monolithic solid, thereby permanently fixing the shear displacement and converting the flexible stack into a rigid structural component." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
