ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_Core_Materials_Extraction_The_Red_Mud_Foundation ex:lignolux_001_method_for_synthesis_of_magnetic_cermet_conductor_skins "A method for manufacturing a high-frequency conductive composite, comprising the application of a lignin-based slurry containing iron oxide nanoparticles onto a metal substrate, followed by Flash Joule Heating (FJH) to simultaneously reduce the iron oxide to metallic nodules and graphitize the lignin into turbostratic graphene, resulting in a magnetically aligned, oxidation-resistant conductive skin." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_Core_Materials_Extraction_The_Red_Mud_Foundation ex:lignolux_001_method_for_synthesis_of_magnetic_cermet_conductor_skins "A method for manufacturing a high-frequency conductive composite, comprising the application of a lignin-based slurry containing iron oxide nanoparticles onto a metal substrate, followed by Flash Joule Heating (FJH) to simultaneously reduce the iron oxide to metallic nodules and graphitize the lignin into turbostratic graphene, resulting in a magnetically aligned, oxidation-resistant conductive skin." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_Core_Materials_Extraction_The_Red_Mud_Foundation ex:lignolux_002_zerowaste_manufacturing_of_electrical_components "A continuous manufacturing process wherein bauxite residue (red mud) is subjected to hydrogen plasma reduction to yield iron nodules, scandium-enriched slag, and alumino-silicate microspheres, which are subsequently processed in-line to form, respectively, magnetic alignment particles, conductor alloy dopants, and ceramic fireproofing fillers." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_Core_Materials_Extraction_The_Red_Mud_Foundation ex:lignolux_002_zerowaste_manufacturing_of_electrical_components "A continuous manufacturing process wherein bauxite residue (red mud) is subjected to hydrogen plasma reduction to yield iron nodules, scandium-enriched slag, and alumino-silicate microspheres, which are subsequently processed in-line to form, respectively, magnetic alignment particles, conductor alloy dopants, and ceramic fireproofing fillers." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_Core_Materials_Extraction_The_Red_Mud_Foundation ex:lignolux_003_fjhassisted_solubility_enhancement_of_rare_earth_elements "A method for extracting critical minerals from bauxite residue, comprising rapid resistive heating (Flash Joule Heating) to induce thermal shock and phase separation, rendering rare earth oxides (Scandium/Yttrium) water-soluble for low-energy hydrometallurgical extraction." .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_I_Core_Materials_Extraction_The_Red_Mud_Foundation ex:lignolux_003_fjhassisted_solubility_enhancement_of_rare_earth_elements "A method for extracting critical minerals from bauxite residue, comprising rapid resistive heating (Flash Joule Heating) to induce thermal shock and phase separation, rendering rare earth oxides (Scandium/Yttrium) water-soluble for low-energy hydrometallurgical extraction." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
