ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_VI_Manufacturing_Facility_Architecture_Expanded ex:lignolux_028_integrated_multistream_conversion_of_bauxite_residue "An industrial system architecture wherein a single mineral waste feedstock (e.g., bauxite residue) is differentiated via high-temperature plasma reduction into at least three simultaneous functional streams: a metallic conductor stream (Iron/Aluminum/Scandium), a ceramic insulator stream (Alumino-Silicates/Titanium Carbide), and a rare-earth dopant stream (Yttrium/Cerium), which are routed directly into parallel continuous manufacturing lines to form a unified composite product without intermediate solidification or transport. _(Protects the \"One Input, Three Outputs\" logic, regardless of how you power it.)_" .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_VI_Manufacturing_Facility_Architecture_Expanded ex:lignolux_028_integrated_multistream_conversion_of_bauxite_residue "An industrial system architecture wherein a single mineral waste feedstock (e.g., bauxite residue) is differentiated via high-temperature plasma reduction into at least three simultaneous functional streams: a metallic conductor stream (Iron/Aluminum/Scandium), a ceramic insulator stream (Alumino-Silicates/Titanium Carbide), and a rare-earth dopant stream (Yttrium/Cerium), which are routed directly into parallel continuous manufacturing lines to form a unified composite product without intermediate solidification or transport. _(Protects the \"One Input, Three Outputs\" logic, regardless of how you power it.)_" >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_VI_Manufacturing_Facility_Architecture_Expanded ex:lignolux_029_closedloop_inductive_energy_recovery_network "A power distribution topology for pulsed-load manufacturing facilities (e.g., fusion reactors or flash joule heating plants), comprising a high-inductance primary load coupled to a low-inductance busbar network and a distributed capacitive storage bank, configured to capture the back-electromotive force (Back-EMF) from the primary load collapse and recirculate it for the subsequent pulse cycle, thereby decoupling the peak process energy demand from the external utility grid. _(Protects the \"Exhale/Inhale\" power circuit, even if they aren't using red mud.)_" .
<< ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_VI_Manufacturing_Facility_Architecture_Expanded ex:lignolux_029_closedloop_inductive_energy_recovery_network "A power distribution topology for pulsed-load manufacturing facilities (e.g., fusion reactors or flash joule heating plants), comprising a high-inductance primary load coupled to a low-inductance busbar network and a distributed capacitive storage bank, configured to capture the back-electromotive force (Back-EMF) from the primary load collapse and recirculate it for the subsequent pulse cycle, thereby decoupling the peak process energy demand from the external utility grid. _(Protects the \"Exhale/Inhale\" power circuit, even if they aren't using red mud.)_" >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
