ex:Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary ex:hasDataTable ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26 .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_0 a ex:TableRow .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26 ex:hasRow ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_0 .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_0 ex:Variant "Cermet-Z™(EV Motor)" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_0 ex:Bend_Radius "3x Diameter(Ultra-Flexible)" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_0 ex:Limiting_Factor "Turbostratic Slip" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_0 ex:Why "Motor Windings.The graphene skin is \"turbostratic\" (disordered layers), allowing the atomic sheets to slide over each other like a deck of cards when bent. It survives the tight turns inside a motor stator." .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_1 a ex:TableRow .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26 ex:hasRow ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_1 .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_1 ex:Variant "Hybrid-Sc™(Grid Cable)" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_1 ex:Bend_Radius "15x Diameter(Rigid)" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_1 ex:Limiting_Factor "Scandium Lattice" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_1 ex:Why "Tower Spans.The core is heavily alloyed with Scandium to make it stiff (like steel). It is designednotto bend or sag under wind/ice loads." .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_2 a ex:TableRow .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26 ex:hasRow ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_2 .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_2 ex:Variant "Redux-Shield™(Safety)" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_2 ex:Bend_Radius "8x Diameter(Stiff)" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_2 ex:Limiting_Factor "Ceramic Armor" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Cables_Method_vs_Application_File_Summary_26_Row_2 ex:Why "Conduits.The jacket is 80% Ceramic Microspheres (Rock). It is flexible enough to snake through a factory tunnel, but if you bend it too sharp, the ceramic matrix will fracture (though the core remains safe)." .
