ex:Green_Fluids_Gear_and_Heat_Pump_What_140_bar_Ethyl_Lactate_Enables a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "1\\. What 140 bar + Ethyl Lactate Enables" .
ex:Green_Fluids_Gear_and_Heat_Pump_What_140_bar_Ethyl_Lactate_Enables ex:molecular_forcing_eliminating_microvoids "At 140 bar, the solvent's surface tension is drastically reduced. It can penetrate the \"nanopores\" of the Lignin Carbon Fiber (LCF) and the dense 2DPA1 matrix. This ensures that every fiber is completely encapsulated by the resin, eliminating the micro-voids that usually cause leaks in high-pressure  $CO_{2}$  systems." .
<< ex:Green_Fluids_Gear_and_Heat_Pump_What_140_bar_Ethyl_Lactate_Enables ex:molecular_forcing_eliminating_microvoids "At 140 bar, the solvent's surface tension is drastically reduced. It can penetrate the \"nanopores\" of the Lignin Carbon Fiber (LCF) and the dense 2DPA1 matrix. This ensures that every fiber is completely encapsulated by the resin, eliminating the micro-voids that usually cause leaks in high-pressure  $CO_{2}$  systems." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Green_Fluids_Gear_and_Heat_Pump_What_140_bar_Ethyl_Lactate_Enables ex:hydrostatic_alignment_of_2dpa1 "Pressure acts as a physical \"press\" on the 2D sheets. By maintaining 140 bar during the initial cure, you force the" .
