ex:Photon_s_Phase_Fingerprint_on_Particles_The_Yield_Bottleneck ex:stanford_yield "In a monolithic stack, a defect in Layer 2 ruins the entire 12-layer stack. Because it is silicon-based, these defects are permanent. Yield drops exponentially with the number of layers because you cannot \"fix\" a transistor once it’s buried under five levels of interconnects." .
