ex:Photon_s_Phase_Fingerprint_on_Particles_Section_1 ex:abstract "Current quantum processing unit (QPU) scaling is hindered by two convergent bottlenecks: the high capital expenditure (CAPEX) of silicon/niobium foundries and the \"Routing Noise Ceiling\" (-20 dB) of standard crossbar interconnects. We propose the" .
