ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_Why_LCS_still_doesnt_fix_LigninCOF ex:the_reason "The laser can remove material (subtractive), but it cannot _force_ a messy polymer to wrap into a perfect helix (additive). If you start with Lignin (disordered blob), the LCS laser can burn away the metallic tubes, but the remaining semiconducting tubes will still be coated in a disordered blob of lignin, resulting in poor bandgap control and high scattering (noise)." .
