ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Physics a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "Why they Align" .
ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Physics ex:dielectrophoresis_dep "Because the CNT is highly conductive and the cellulose/lignin is insulating, an AC electric field induces a dipole moment in the tube. The tube acts like a compass needle and rotates to align parallel to the field lines." .
<< ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Physics ex:dielectrophoresis_dep "Because the CNT is highly conductive and the cellulose/lignin is insulating, an AC electric field induces a dipole moment in the tube. The tube acts like a compass needle and rotates to align parallel to the field lines." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Physics ex:the_wrapper_effect "The cellulose wrapper actually _helps_ here. It prevents the tubes from bundling together (which kills alignment) and keeps them individual so they can rotate freely." .
<< ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Physics ex:the_wrapper_effect "The cellulose wrapper actually _helps_ here. It prevents the tubes from bundling together (which kills alignment) and keeps them individual so they can rotate freely." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
