ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Problem a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "\"The Lignin Drag\"" .
ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Problem ex:viscosity "Lignin vitrimers are thick and viscous even before they fully set. Rotating a nanotube in water is like spinning a spoon in tea; rotating it in lignin is like spinning a spoon in cold honey. You need massive field strengths (\\>$10 V/$\\\\mum) to overcome this drag." .
<< ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Problem ex:viscosity "Lignin vitrimers are thick and viscous even before they fully set. Rotating a nanotube in water is like spinning a spoon in tea; rotating it in lignin is like spinning a spoon in cold honey. You need massive field strengths (\\>$10 V/$\\\\mum) to overcome this drag." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Problem ex:steric_hindrance "Lignin is a large, bulky, hyper-branched polymer. It physically gets in the way. As the CNT tries to rotate, it bumps into the lignin molecular branches, preventing perfect alignment." .
<< ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Problem ex:steric_hindrance "Lignin is a large, bulky, hyper-branched polymer. It physically gets in the way. As the CNT tries to rotate, it bumps into the lignin molecular branches, preventing perfect alignment." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
