ex:CNT_Bandgap_Creation_with_Lignin_Vitrimer_The_Edge_between_LCS_Stepper_and_Printed_Bragg_Reflector_DMD ex:what_is_a_bragg_reflector "It is a mirror made not of metal, but of many stacked layers of transparent materials with different refractive indices. As light passes through, it reflects off each interface. If the layer thicknesses are tuned exactly to a quarter-wavelength of the light, these reflections constructively interfere, creating a near-perfect mirror (99.9%+ reflectivity)." .
