ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:a_the_bandgap_problem_graphene "Graphene is a \"semi-metal\" or \"zero-gap semiconductor.\" It conducts electricity _too_ well." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:a_the_bandgap_problem_graphene "Graphene is a \"semi-metal\" or \"zero-gap semiconductor.\" It conducts electricity _too_ well." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:silicon "You can turn it ON (1) and OFF (0) easily." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:silicon "You can turn it ON (1) and OFF (0) easily." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:graphene "It is incredibly hard to turn OFF. Current leaks through even when \"off.\"" .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:graphene "It is incredibly hard to turn OFF. Current leaks through even when \"off.\"" >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:the_fix "To create a bandgap, you have to constrain graphene into incredibly thin strips (Graphene Nanoribbons) or stress it. This fabrication requires precision that currently exceeds even EUV capabilities at commercial scale." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:the_fix "To create a bandgap, you have to constrain graphene into incredibly thin strips (Graphene Nanoribbons) or stress it. This fabrication requires precision that currently exceeds even EUV capabilities at commercial scale." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:result "Without a reliable bandgap, you cannot make efficient logic gates (CPUs/GPUs) without massive power leakage, defeating the efficiency purpose." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:result "Without a reliable bandgap, you cannot make efficient logic gates (CPUs/GPUs) without massive power leakage, defeating the efficiency purpose." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:b_the_purity_and_alignment_problem_cnts "Carbon Nanotubes (CNTs) _do_ have a bandgap and are excellent semiconductors. The problem is entropy." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:b_the_purity_and_alignment_problem_cnts "Carbon Nanotubes (CNTs) _do_ have a bandgap and are excellent semiconductors. The problem is entropy." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:metallic_vs_semiconducting "When you grow CNTs, you get a mix: some act like copper wire (metallic), some like silicon (semiconducting). If a single \"metallic\" CNT lands in a transistor, it causes a short circuit." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:metallic_vs_semiconducting "When you grow CNTs, you get a mix: some act like copper wire (metallic), some like silicon (semiconducting). If a single \"metallic\" CNT lands in a transistor, it causes a short circuit." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:alignment "Silicon utilizes a single crystal boule. CNTs are like a pile of spaghetti. To make a chip, you need billions of nanotubes perfectly aligned in parallel. While \"laser shocking\" and fluidic alignment help, getting 99.999999% purity (required for chips with billions of transistors) is not yet solved at scale." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Technical_Hurdle ex:alignment "Silicon utilizes a single crystal boule. CNTs are like a pile of spaghetti. To make a chip, you need billions of nanotubes perfectly aligned in parallel. While \"laser shocking\" and fluidic alignment help, getting 99.999999% purity (required for chips with billions of transistors) is not yet solved at scale." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
