ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "2\\. Why Hyperscalers Can't Switch Yet (The Density Problem)" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem ex:the_spaghetti_factor "To make a high-performance chip, carbon nanotubes must be perfectly aligned (like uncooked pasta in a box)." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem ex:the_spaghetti_factor "To make a high-performance chip, carbon nanotubes must be perfectly aligned (like uncooked pasta in a box)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem ex:current_process "When we \"print\" or solution-process CNTs (like on paper/silk), they land randomly (like cooked spaghetti). Electrons have to hop from tube to tube, which creates heat and slows down calculation." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem ex:current_process "When we \"print\" or solution-process CNTs (like on paper/silk), they land randomly (like cooked spaghetti). Electrons have to hop from tube to tube, which creates heat and slows down calculation." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem ex:hyperscale_requirement "For an AI chip, you need 99.9999% pure semiconducting tubes, all aligned within 1-2 degrees. We can currently do this on small scales (using \"fluidic alignment\" or \"dimension-limited self-alignment\"), but not on the wafer-scale needed for mass production." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem ex:hyperscale_requirement "For an AI chip, you need 99.9999% pure semiconducting tubes, all aligned within 1-2 degrees. We can currently do this on small scales (using \"fluidic alignment\" or \"dimension-limited self-alignment\"), but not on the wafer-scale needed for mass production." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem ex:the_metallic_contamination "Roughly 33% of grown CNTs are \"metallic\" (conductors) rather than semiconductors. If _one_ metallic tube bridges a transistor's source and drain, that transistor is permanently \"ON.\" In a chip with 50 billion transistors, even a 0.000001% failure rate means a dead chip. We have not yet perfected a cheap industrial way to filter these out perfectly." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Why_Hyperscalers_Cant_Switch_Yet_The_Density_Problem ex:the_metallic_contamination "Roughly 33% of grown CNTs are \"metallic\" (conductors) rather than semiconductors. If _one_ metallic tube bridges a transistor's source and drain, that transistor is permanently \"ON.\" In a chip with 50 billion transistors, even a 0.000001% failure rate means a dead chip. We have not yet perfected a cheap industrial way to filter these out perfectly." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
    ex:extractionSource "MyST-Parser-Regex" .
