    rdfs:label "Flax for Sodium-Ion Batteries (Hard Carbon)" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Application_1 ex:the_mechanism "Because flax has higher cellulose content, when you pyrolyze it (burn it without oxygen), it doesn't graphitize easily. Instead, it forms \"cards\" of carbon that are stacked messily. Sodium ions can wedge themselves into the gaps between these cards." .
