ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Tech_Ingredients_Comparison a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "Silicone Oil vs. Green Fluid" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Tech_Ingredients_Comparison ex:why_your_fluid_wins_for_active_cooling "Silicone oil is great for a _static_ pad (thermal paste), but terrible for a _flowing_ loop because it holds very little heat per gram. Water (even mixed with glycol) holds 2.5x more heat than oil. By adding Lignin-stabilized CNTs, you boost the _thermal conductivity_ (how fast heat moves) without sacrificing the _heat capacity_ (how much heat it holds)." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_The_Tech_Ingredients_Comparison ex:why_your_fluid_wins_for_active_cooling "Silicone oil is great for a _static_ pad (thermal paste), but terrible for a _flowing_ loop because it holds very little heat per gram. Water (even mixed with glycol) holds 2.5x more heat than oil. By adding Lignin-stabilized CNTs, you boost the _thermal conductivity_ (how fast heat moves) without sacrificing the _heat capacity_ (how much heat it holds)." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
