ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Enhancing_ShearThinning_Behavior_Energy_Efficiency a iof:PlannedProcess ;
    rdfs:label "2\\. Enhancing Shear-Thinning Behavior (Energy Efficiency)" .
ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Enhancing_ShearThinning_Behavior_Energy_Efficiency ex:the_benefit "A shear-thinning fluid is thick and viscous at rest or under low shear (like when the system is cold or off). This prevents settling and provides a strong protective barrier (thick film). However, when the system starts and high shear is applied (like when the fluid passes through a gear mesh or a pump), the internal  $CNF$  network temporarily collapses, causing the viscosity to drop immediately." .
<< ex:Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_Enhancing_ShearThinning_Behavior_Energy_Efficiency ex:the_benefit "A shear-thinning fluid is thick and viscous at rest or under low shear (like when the system is cold or off). This prevents settling and provides a strong protective barrier (thick film). However, when the system starts and high shear is applied (like when the fluid passes through a gear mesh or a pump), the internal  $CNF$  network temporarily collapses, causing the viscosity to drop immediately." >> ex:confidence 0.8 ;
