ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_0 a ex:TableRow .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15 ex:hasRow ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_0 .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_0 ex:Component_Produced "Silicon Carbide (SiC)" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_0 ex:Biorefinery_Feedstock_Waste_Stream "Rice Straw/Husk Ash" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_0 ex:Synergy_Function "The ash residue from burning rice husks contains high concentrations of amorphoussilica (SiO2​). This can be mixed with theCarbon Charfrom the solar pyrolysis and heated to1,500∘C+ to create high-performanceSiCceramics." .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_1 a ex:TableRow .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15 ex:hasRow ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_1 .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_1 ex:Component_Produced "Porous Bioceramics" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_1 ex:Biorefinery_Feedstock_Waste_Stream "Lignin" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_1 ex:Synergy_Function "Lignin is a binding agent. It can be mixed with ceramic powders (likeAl2​O3​orZrO2​) and then pyrolyzed. The lignin burns out, leaving behind highly porous, high-strengthceramic scaffolds(ideal for lightweight structural components or advanced filters)." .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_2 a ex:TableRow .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15 ex:hasRow ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_2 .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_2 ex:Component_Produced "High-Purity Silica" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_2 ex:Biorefinery_Feedstock_Waste_Stream "CNF Waste Water" .
ex:Table_Carbon_Chips_Hurdles_and_Future_File_Summary_15_Row_2 ex:Synergy_Function "The process used to extract Nanocellulose often leaves behind silica rich water. This can be harvested and calcinated in the high-heat zone to produce high-puritysilica fillerfor ceramic composites." .
